由于你的慵懒，我不得不另找他人来接手这项任务。这个机会我们已经等很久了！我们不能就这样让这机会溜走。或许你不是个能在危险时刻为联邦出力的人……？

{[character]agentID.name}

messages.en:
{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Your lack of initiative has allowed that shipment of Vitoc to get away! We have waited years for this opportunity! Perhaps you're not the right kind of person to be a Federation capsuleer. Maybe the capitalistic Caldari would be more suited to your temperament... <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

messages.zh:
{[character]player.name}，

由于你的慵懒，我不得不另找他人来接手这项任务。这个机会我们已经等很久了！我们不能就这样让这机会溜走。或许你不是个能在危险时刻为联邦出力的人。也许资本主义盛行的加达里才是你的归宿……

{[character]agentID.name}

messages.en:
{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
It seems some Caldari agent managed to get to our man, thanks to your lack of initiative. Not only that, but they took out the whole outpost, along with all the research we had going on there. This is quite a setback, all no thanks to you. Well done. Well done. <br><br> 
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
I found someone else willing to handle this. Your loss is someone else's gain. Could have been your account full of ISK. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Luckily, I found someone else to handle this. Your lack of initiative would have allowed that insane Amarrian terrorist to detonate a bomb on the Crystal Boulevard! Perhaps you're not the right kind of person to be a capsuleer in service to the Federation. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Your lack of initiative has allowed that filthy Amarrian to escape with a load of Gallente citizens! You could have stopped him! Are you you're fit to fly in Gallente space!? <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
You have failed to recapture the fugitive Geeral, formerly of House Tash-Murkon. Thanks to your lack of courage, he was to escape to Gallente space. If the Amarrian Empire's financial well-being takes a downturn in the next few days, you will know why. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
You have failed to recapture the fugitive Geeral, formerly of House Tash-Murkon. Thanks to your lack of courage, he was to escape to Gallente space. If the Amarrian Empire's financial well-being takes a downturn in the next few days, you will know why. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Thanks to your lack of initiative, I was able to find someone much more qualified. Take your cowardice and go back to hauling slaves. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Thanks to your lack of initiative, I was able to find someone much more qualified. Take your cowardice and go back to hauling slaves. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Thanks to your lack of attention, Admiral Meledier was recaptured by his own people and imprisoned. Perhaps you should go back to driving a garbage scow, where you belong. All the Empire will know of your failure. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Thanks to your lack of attention, Admiral Meledier was recaptured by his own people and imprisoned. Perhaps you should go back to driving a garbage scow, where you belong. All the Empire will know of your failure. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
You do not take things very seriously, do you? Because you have waited so long to respond to my offer, I have been forced to find someone else to take the job. Don't expect me to contact you again unless you prove that you are more trustworthy. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Because you waited so long to move, the crooked customs official was able to allow another shipment of slaves into the Federation. Not only that, but he caught wind of our operation and fled. Nice work. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br> 
Have you ever had a really annoying itch that just won't go away? Well, that's what this satellite it to me. And those claylickers keep making it worse. I'm getting someone else to get rid of it for me. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br> 
You really must hate me, don't you? Those soil-sniffers keep bothering me, asking me when you're going to get rid of that broadcast satellite. And I can't stand them calling me anymore. I'm sending someone else to take care of it. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
I know that none of us really cares about that little claylicker, but this job needs to get taken care of. Since you obviously can't be bothered, I've sent someone else. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Ok, the first time that rock-flea sent me a message asking where you were, I laughed. The second time, I chuckled. The third time, I started to get angry. Now, I'm ready to kill someone. Before I snap, I'm sending someone else to pick up the blowhard. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
It seems that apathy is the better part of valor in this case. Our Caldari Navy officer fled rather than be ground into dust. It would have been better if he were trashed, but, oh well. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
Well, it turns out that the Caldari officer wasn't all that concerned with his revenge. He's already packed up and moved out. It's a shame we couldn't punish him, but it's out of my hair, so whatever. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
And here I thought you a decent sort, the type of pilot who doesn't leave a poor agent hanging. I've had to hire another pilot who understands how to treat me right. <br><br> 
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
I was absolutely crushed when I heard you failed to destroy that Caldari cruiser,. Just <i>crushed</i>. I hope you're dead so you don't disappoint me anymore. I really, <i>really</i> mean it. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}, <br><br>
I'd like to think that you died heroically trying to recover that log book from the Guristas. But something tells me you just couldn't be bothered. To that end, I've notified my superiors of your failure, just to be on the safe side. Have a super day! <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}: <br><br>
This may come as a shock, but the universe doesn't revolve around you. 'Neither do I — which is why I hired someone else to obtain that data chip for me. Tough luck, chump. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}

{[character]player.name}: <br><br>
Remember me? You were supposed to get that data chip for me so we could decipher that message we intercepted? This tip any sensors with you? Yeah, didn't think so. Thanks for becoming my new definition for failure. <br><br>
{[character]agentID.name}
